c career, he rose to become one of the most prominent and influential cultural icons in South Korea, with many referring to him as \"the President of Culture\". Following a brief stint in the heavy metal band Sinawe, Taiji formed Seo Taiji and Boys in 1991 with whom he found immediate success.","title":"Seo Taiji","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seo_Taiji"}},"Q43088724":{"id":"Q43088724","name":"Kim Seong-lee","ko":"김성리","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Kim Seong-ri"],"birth":"1994-04-06","death":"","birthplace":"Andong","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer"],"debut":"","agencies":[],"groups":[{"id":"Q41399213","name":"Rainz","start":"","end":""}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/seongri0406/"},"photo":null,"bio":null},"Q489108":{"id":"Q489108","name":"Chae Yeon","ko":"채연","birthName":"이채연","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Lee Chae-yeon","Lee Jin-sook","Chae-yeon","Chaeyeon","Lee Chae Yeon","Lee Chaeyeon","Chae Yun","Chae-yun"],"birth":"1978-12-10","death":"","birthplace":"Seoul","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer"],"debut":"2001","agencies":[{"name":"Media Line Entertainment","id":"Q59454113","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/chaeyeon_lee/","x":"https://x.com/chaeyeon_lee","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/96e5f3bc-27b8-4515-8b0e-a56508aa4713"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Lee Jin-sook, better known as Chae Yeon, is a South Korean singer who rose to fame with her hit single \"Two of Us\" in 2004.","title":"Chae Yeon","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chae_Yeon"}},"Q489556":{"id":"Q489556","name":"Amber Liu","ko":"엠버","birthName":"Amber Josephine Liu","birthNameEn":"Amber Josephine Liu","aliases":[],"birth":"1992-09-18","death":"","birthplace":"Los Angeles","nationality":["United States","Taiwan"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer","dancer","composer","television actor","songwriter","taekwondo athlete"],"debut":"2009","agencies":[{"name":"SM Entertainment","id":"Q483938","start":"","end":""},{"name":"United Talent Agency","id":"Q7893586","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q344286","name":"f(x)","start":"","end":""}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/ajol_llama/","x":"https://x.com/llama_ajol","youtube":"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCD-aVzvsQsFizfMSuUSN9cA","spotify":"https://open.spotify.com/artist/6vPzAqZDXQgLTEn8pjp4jY","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/aff352dd-b20e-4349-a01b-cc01d53e077b"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Amber Josephine Liu, also known mononymously as Amber, is an American singer, rapper, and songwriter. She debuted as a member of the South Korean girl group f(x) in September 2009. In 2015, she became the first f(x) member to make a solo debut with the release of her first extended play Beautiful and has since released solo singles in Korean, English, and Mandarin. In July 2018, she joined Steel Wool Entertainment following her original label SM Entertainment's joint partnership with Steel Wool to manage her American activities. In September 2019, she left SM and exclusively signed with Steel Wool prior to the release of her 2020 extended play X.","title":"Amber Liu (singer)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amber_Liu_%28singer%29"}},"Q494996":{"id":"Q494996","name":"Goo Hara","ko":"구하라","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Goo Ha Ra","Gu Ha-ra","Gu Hara","Gu Ha Ra","Koo Ha-ra","Koo Ha Ra","Koo Hara","Ku Ha-ra"],"birth":"1991-01-03","death":"2019-11-24","birthplace":"Gwangju","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["actor","singer","pop singer"],"debut":"2008","agencies":[{"name":"Universal Music Group","id":"Q38903","start":"","end":""},{"name":"DSP Media","id":"Q489428","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q124459","name":"Kara","start":"2008","end":"2016"}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/koohara__/","x":"https://x.com/_sweethara","youtube":"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCZF2SBc7Zz5NOH9STpz2F7A","spotify":"https://open.spotify.com/artist/0YK9cO0HbCzcBe4P1CH4cj","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/526ce891-0659-46d8-b1cb-b2c72ab3dba4"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Goo Hara, also known mononymously as Hara, was a South Korean singer and actress. She was a member of the K-pop girl group Kara, and had also appeared in television dramas including City Hunter (2011). She made her debut as a soloist in July 2015 with the release of her EP Alohara (Can You Feel It?). After Kara disbanded in 2016, she continued her solo career at another agency, KeyEast. In June 2019, she signed with Production Ogi and continued her solo activities in Japan where she was well received by fans. Her last release was maxi single \"Midnight Queen\" on September 19, 2019. In November 2019, she embarked on a Japanese mini tour to support the album.","title":"Goo Hara","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goo_Hara"}},"Q5512084":{"id":"Q5512084","name":"G.O","ko":"지오","birthName":"정병희","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Jung Byung Hee"],"birth":"1987-11-06","death":"","birthplace":"Changwon","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer","actor"],"debut":"2009","agencies":[{"name":"J. Tune Camp","id":"Q16850770","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q499183","name":"MBLAQ","start":"","end":""}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/jung_g_o/","x":"https://x.com/MBLAQGO","spotify":"https://open.spotify.com/artist/45b9wd8woWmJemezwAQfa6","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/4ae2e2df-c301-492b-89f8-77367e3239bf"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Jung Byung-hee, known professionally as G.O, is a South Korean singer-songwriter and actor. He is best known as a member of South Korean boy band MBLAQ.","title":"G.O (singer)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/G.O_%28singer%29"}},"Q60668820":{"id":"Q60668820","name":"Woo Ami","ko":"우아미","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Ami"],"birth":"1994-06-05","death":"","birthplace":"Ulsan","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer"],"debut":"","agencies":[],"groups":[{"id":"Q28700240","name":"WANNA.B","start":"2015","end":""}],"links":{},"photo":null,"bio":null},"Q60991892":{"id":"Q60991892","name":"Jinjin","ko":"진진","birthName":"박진우","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["JinJin","Park Jin Woo","Park Jin-woo"],"birth":"1996-03-15","death":"","birthplace":"Ilsan","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer","rapper","actor","dancer","singer-songwriter","record producer"],"debut":"2016","agencies":[{"name":"Fantagio","id":"Q13424955","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q23004252","name":"Astro","start":"","end":""}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/ast_jinjin/","spotify":"https://open.spotify.com/artist/4XgriSgrYFwwrNINHj3hd5","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/6b3ff422-1786-409a-ade5-d3e7b131f717"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Park Jin-woo, known professionally as Jinjin (진진), is a South Korean rapper, singer, songwriter and dancer. He is the leader of South Korean boy group Astro and former member of its sub unit Jinjin & Rocky with ex-member Rocky under the label Fantagio.","title":"Jinjin","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jinjin"}},"Q84324500":{"id":"Q84324500","name":"Jee Won","ko":"지원","birthName":"Kim Ji-won","birthNameEn":"Kim Ji-won","aliases":["Jeewon","Kim Ji-won","Jiwon","ZZONE"],"birth":"1999-04-01","death":"","birthplace":"Seoul","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer"],"debut":"2017","agencies":[{"name":"C9 Entertainment","id":"Q16167317","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q39074586","name":"Good Day","start":"2017","end":"2019"},{"id":"Q84311821","name":"Cignature","start":"2020","end":"2024"},{"id":"Q137734516","name":"Latency","start":"","end":""}],"links":{"musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/5a28b6ba-3021-4c5e-8659-3a08a2c71a09"},"photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/59/Jeewon_of_Latency%2C_2026.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jeewon_of_Latency,_2026.jpg","author":"mang2goon","license":"CC BY 4.0"},"bio":{"text":"Kim Ji-won, known professionally as Jeewon (지원) and as a soloist by the stage name ZZONE (지지원), is a South Korean singer and guitarist. She was the guitarist for the band Latency and a former member of girl groups Good Day and Cignature. She is known for her viral performance at the 2024 Waterbomb Festival.","title":"ZZONE","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ZZONE"}},"Q85881428":{"id":"Q85881428","name":"Yoo Tae-yang","ko":"유태양","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Taeyang"],"birth":"1997-02-28","death":"","birthplace":"","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer","musician"],"debut":"","agencies":[],"groups":[{"id":"Q26856852","name":"SF9","start":"","end":""}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/taeyang_0228/","tiktok":"https://www.tiktok.com/@taeyang_0228"},"photo":null,"bio":null}}}